cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use GAUNTLET, please cite it as below. GAUNTLET is a research prototype; its results concern
  hand-written reference implementations, mutants and synthetic fixtures (beyond one demonstration run of a
  single Gemini-generated candidate, no AI coding agent has been evaluated) and have not been independently
  reproduced.
type: software
title: "GAUNTLET: adversarial evaluation of database-migration code under concurrency, partial failure and retries"
version: "0.4.1"
date-released: "2026-11-16"
license: Apache-2.0
authors:
  - family-names: Tantipudi
    given-names: Snigdha
abstract: >-
  GAUNTLET is a research instrument that tests whether online schema-migration code that passes
  conventional functional tests stays correct under adversarial execution: statement-level interleavings
  of concurrent legacy and new application versions, process crashes, lost responses, retries and
  repeated or resumed migration steps. A controller gates every SQL statement of every actor process, so
  schedules are exact and replayable, and an oracle independent of the implementation judges each run from
  the client-visible ledger and raw database snapshots. It includes differential testing, bounded schedule
  exploration, failure minimization and experiment reports with hashed evidence manifests.
keywords:
  - database migration
  - schema migration
  - concurrency testing
  - fault injection
  - linearizability
  - AI coding agents
  - evaluation
